Capstone Challenge: Cloud Flight Simulator
Problem Statement
Cloud learning platforms today rely heavily on static labs where every learner performs the same tasks regardless of their experience level, strengths, or learning progress. This results in repetitive learning experiences, poor engagement, and limited assessment of real-world problem-solving abilities.
Your team has been tasked with building Cloud Flight Simulator, an AI-powered platform that generates dynamic cloud challenges based on a learner's selected domain, skill level, and performance history.
Instead of presenting predefined instructions, the platform should create realistic cloud scenarios, provision a temporary Google Cloud environment, monitor learner actions, assess progress automatically, and adapt subsequent challenges based on performance.
The objective is to create a personalized cloud learning experience where every learner receives unique scenarios and is evaluated based on actual cloud activity rather than manual submissions.

User Journey
A learner selects:
Learning Track (Compute, Storage, Networking, Security, DevOps, Architecture)
Difficulty Level (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced)
Based on the selection, the platform generates a unique cloud mission and provisions a temporary Google Cloud environment.
As the learner performs actions within the cloud environment, the system continuously evaluates resource creation, configurations, and task completion.
Upon successful completion, the platform generates a score, provides feedback, and recommends or creates the next challenge based on learner performance.

Deliverables
1. Learner Portal
A web application where learners can:
Register and login
Select cloud domain and difficulty level
Launch challenges
View progress and scores
Review completed missions

2. Dynamic Scenario Generator
An AI-powered engine that generates cloud missions based on:
Selected learning track
Difficulty level
Previous performance
Completed challenges
Every mission should contain:
Business context
Objectives
Success criteria
Time limit

3. Temporary Cloud Environment
The platform should provision a temporary Google Cloud environment for each challenge and automatically remove resources after challenge completion or timeout.

4. Automated Evaluation Engine
The platform should evaluate learner actions by inspecting actual cloud resources and configurations.
Evaluation must be based on the state of cloud resources rather than manual submissions.

5. AI Feedback and Recommendation Engine
The system should:
Provide intelligent feedback
Highlight mistakes
Suggest improvements
Recommend the next challenge

6. Progress and Performance Dashboard
Learners should be able to view:
Completed challenges
Scores
Success rate
Learning progression
Skill growth over time

7. Observability and Tracing
All AI-generated scenarios, evaluations, recommendations, and decision-making workflows must be traceable using LangSmith.
The platform should capture:
Scenario generation traces
Evaluation traces
Feedback generation traces
Recommendation traces

8. Audit and Activity Tracking
The platform should maintain a complete record of:
Learner actions
Cloud resource changes
Mission attempts
Evaluation outcomes
AI-generated decisions

Mandatory Features
Authentication and authorization
Dynamic scenario generation
Google Cloud integration
Temporary environment provisioning
Automated challenge validation
AI-powered evaluation
AI-powered recommendations
LangSmith tracing
Audit logging
Progress dashboard
